WEBVTT

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:42.686
The first U-17 Japanese team versus

00:01:42.686 --> 00:01:46.731
second string shuffle match will now begin.

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:49.776
Representing the U-17 Japanese team are

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:56.241
doubles team No. 10, Jusaburoh Mori,
and No. 9, Tsukimitsu Ochi.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:03.498
I'm up first!

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.875
Let's go, Niou!

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:07.961
I've been waiting for this.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.839
Representing the second string are

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:13.341
Keigo Atobe and Masaharu Niou.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.055
Don't let your guard down, Atobe.

00:02:19.055 --> 00:02:21.016
Huh? "Let your guard down"?

00:02:21.016 --> 00:02:22.934
What language is that?

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:28.940
"The Strongest Pair"

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:37.574
I never thought I'd get to see
Tezuka and Atobe play doubles here.

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:42.579
It's actually Niou-<i>san</i>, though.

00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:46.750
Hey, Blue Streaks.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.461
I hear you graduated from Hyotei.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.507
Thanks for making Hyotei a
nationally competitive team.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.426
But...

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:00.764
Hey, are you listening, Blue Streaks?

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.726
Fifteen-love!

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.482
The time for talk is over.

00:03:10.482 --> 00:03:14.694
Focus, or you won't be able to
stop Tsuki-<i>san</i>'s Mach Serves.

00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:17.447
What are you doing, Atobe?

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.865
I told you not to let your guard do--

00:03:21.826 --> 00:03:22.869
Thirty-love!

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:26.664
Wh-What was that?

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:29.459
I couldn't even see the ball.

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:35.173
A perfect flat serve from a
height of 226 centimeters.

00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:38.927
According to my data,
his success rate is 100%.

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:42.764
No one can return it... No.

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:45.684
No one can even react to it.

00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:48.395
He returned it!

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.815
Whoops. You returned that?

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.650
Forty-love!

00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:58.947
That will not turn the tides.

00:04:02.409 --> 00:04:03.410
Game, first string!

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.869
One game to love!

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:07.789
As long as he's got that,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:11.710
they won't be able to break Ochi's serve.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:16.631
Having a good serve makes all the difference.

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:22.429
That's...

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:25.849
Fifteen-love!

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:28.351
The Zero Degree Serve.

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:30.770
Niou...

00:04:31.855 --> 00:04:35.066
...has already learned to hit
the Zero Degree Serve?

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.528
Not bad.

00:04:41.906 --> 00:04:43.324
Interesting.

00:04:43.324 --> 00:04:45.493
He can manage a pro-level serve.

00:04:47.746 --> 00:04:48.621
He returned it!

00:04:52.917 --> 00:04:54.419
Tezuka Zone.

00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:56.838
He's got skills.

00:04:57.172 --> 00:04:58.757
Get in position.

00:04:58.757 --> 00:04:59.966
We'll attack.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:00.925
Too slow!

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.137
Thirty-love!

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:09.059
We are the strongest pair.

00:05:11.436 --> 00:05:12.020
Niou,

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.774
interested in forming the
strongest pair with me?

00:05:16.232 --> 00:05:17.901
The strongest pair?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.946
The first shuffle match will be doubles.

00:05:22.489 --> 00:05:27.118
We'll own that match and take
the wind out of their sails.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.206
Game, second string!

00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:32.457
One game all!

00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:34.376
Game, first string!

00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:35.960
Three games to two!

00:05:37.295 --> 00:05:38.213
Game, second string!

00:05:38.213 --> 00:05:39.631
Three games all!

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.217
Game, first string!

00:05:42.217 --> 00:05:43.968
Five games to four!

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.597
This is turning into a service ace battle.

00:05:48.556 --> 00:05:54.896
The way this is going, the first team to
break its opponent's serve will win.

00:05:57.732 --> 00:05:58.817
Fifteen-love!

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:00.860
Thirty-love!

00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:02.779
Forty-love!

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:05.532
Niou's amazing.

00:06:05.532 --> 00:06:07.200
It's like watching Tezuka himself.

00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:17.836
Whoa, that was close.

00:06:17.836 --> 00:06:19.004
A normal serve, huh?

00:06:19.587 --> 00:06:21.339
Well done.

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:23.717
Now leave the rest to me!

00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:28.930
You're wide open!

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.724
Fugue Towards Disappointment!

00:06:32.183 --> 00:06:33.101
Game, second string!

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:34.644
Five games all!

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.983
He can't serve any more Zero Degrees.

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.905
We'll go for it in the next game.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:52.203
We'll break their serve.

00:06:57.876 --> 00:06:58.752
Whoops!

00:07:07.719 --> 00:07:11.514
If only you guys were a bit stronger.

00:07:11.765 --> 00:07:12.766
Huh?

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.726
I think he just said something.

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:19.314
What? Kabaji?

00:07:21.733 --> 00:07:22.650
Game, second string!

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.402
Six games to five!

00:07:24.402 --> 00:07:25.153
Yes!

00:07:25.653 --> 00:07:29.074
They finally broke the first string's serve.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.785
Well done, Kabaji.

00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:32.827
Yes, sir.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:36.206
How long are you going
to stay as Kabaji, anyway?

00:07:36.206 --> 00:07:37.499
Yes, sir. Puri.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.293
Stay as Tezuka.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.587
It takes only a second to get tripped up.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:44.047
Ribbit.

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:49.844
We've got them now.

00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:53.306
I just need to hold my serve.

00:07:57.519 --> 00:07:58.561
What was that?

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:07.862
What's wrong, Atobe?

00:08:09.572 --> 00:08:10.782
Nothing.

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:21.167
Take this!

00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:23.211
Tannhauser!

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:25.130
Fault!

00:08:27.674 --> 00:08:28.675
Double fault!

00:08:28.675 --> 00:08:30.093
Love-fifteen!

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:34.931
You're kidding me! Atobe hit a double fault?

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.143
Why?

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:39.978
Why don't they go in?

00:08:42.105 --> 00:08:43.106
Double fault!

00:08:43.106 --> 00:08:44.357
Love-forty!

00:08:44.858 --> 00:08:48.278
Something's clearly wrong.

00:08:48.945 --> 00:08:54.284
For Atobe to keep missing
all his serves like this...

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:56.828
Atobe-<i>san</i>, pull yourself together!

00:08:57.245 --> 00:08:58.288
Shut up!

00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:01.708
Double fault!

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:03.335
Game, first string!

00:09:03.335 --> 00:09:04.794
Six games all!

00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:07.881
First set tie-breaker, first string to serve!

00:09:10.425 --> 00:09:12.552
What's wrong with Atobe-<i>san</i>?

00:09:13.011 --> 00:09:14.012
It's the pressure.

00:09:14.346 --> 00:09:18.433
What? Atobe-<i>san</i>, feel pressured? No way!

00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:23.355
There's no one in this world
who doesn't feel pressure.

00:09:24.272 --> 00:09:27.192
"I just need to hold my serve."

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:30.737
That's how small the pressure started out.

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:36.534
But a single glare from
Tsukimitsu Ochi made it grow.

00:09:36.951 --> 00:09:39.913
"If I don't make this, we'll lose."

00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:42.207
"I must make this shot."

00:09:42.791 --> 00:09:47.587
The pressure grew stronger
and threw Atobe off his game.

00:09:49.631 --> 00:09:52.634
His completely unruffled appearance...

00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:56.721
Tsukimitsu Ochi's glare has
made countless players

00:09:56.721 --> 00:10:00.058
lose their cool and taste defeat.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:05.563
It's why they call him the "Mental Assassin."

00:10:10.235 --> 00:10:12.946
Pressure? That doesn't mean a thing.

00:10:12.946 --> 00:10:14.447
I feel exhilarated.

00:10:16.658 --> 00:10:18.743
Whoa! He returned another?

00:10:20.412 --> 00:10:21.329
This is my chance!

00:10:21.913 --> 00:10:25.250
I'll make this shot and
end this unlucky streak!

00:10:29.796 --> 00:10:30.672
Out!

00:10:30.672 --> 00:10:31.965
One-zero, first string!

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.064
Six-zero, first string!

00:10:49.232 --> 00:10:50.358
Again?

00:10:58.616 --> 00:11:00.869
This is absurd! I can't lose now!

00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:02.537
He's going for the poach!

00:11:03.163 --> 00:11:03.788
Seriously?

00:11:04.247 --> 00:11:06.708
The way he's playing, won't he just miss?

00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:08.418
Quiet, peanut gallery!

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:12.339
I can't keep disgracing myself!

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.259
Out!

00:11:16.259 --> 00:11:17.677
Six-one, second string!

00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:18.470
What?

00:11:18.928 --> 00:11:19.888
That's...

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:24.225
Tezuka Phantom.

00:11:24.893 --> 00:11:27.979
Atobe, you don't need
to hit the ball anymore.

00:11:28.438 --> 00:11:31.399
I'll deflect the rest out of the court.

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:36.237
Tsuki-<i>san</i>, watch this!

00:11:37.947 --> 00:11:40.575
The ball's changing its
trajectory and flying loose!

00:11:41.659 --> 00:11:42.327
Out!

00:11:42.327 --> 00:11:43.995
Six-three, second string!

00:11:45.205 --> 00:11:45.872
Out!

00:11:45.872 --> 00:11:47.207
Six-four, second string!

00:11:48.166 --> 00:11:51.753
He's putting massive topspin on the ball

00:11:51.753 --> 00:11:55.548
to deflect all our shots out of the court?

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:58.009
Out!

00:11:58.009 --> 00:11:59.511
Six-five, second string!

00:11:59.761 --> 00:12:02.013
That's it! They're coming back!

00:12:02.013 --> 00:12:03.431
Go!

00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:09.938
He followed up Zero Degree Serves
with continuous Phantoms.

00:12:10.647 --> 00:12:13.858
His elbow is already past its limit.

00:12:14.901 --> 00:12:15.610
Out!

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:17.278
Six all, second string!

00:12:17.278 --> 00:12:20.073
All right! They finally caught up!

00:12:26.454 --> 00:12:27.747
That's enough.

00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:31.793
Pupina.

00:12:31.793 --> 00:12:33.712
My hand slipped, that's all.

00:12:33.712 --> 00:12:35.338
You did well.

00:12:35.338 --> 00:12:37.298
Don't hit any more Phantoms.

00:12:38.091 --> 00:12:40.468
It could affect your career.

00:12:41.928 --> 00:12:43.471
Atobe,

00:12:43.471 --> 00:12:44.889
who am I?

00:12:49.477 --> 00:12:53.148
If this were Kunimitsu Tezuka,
he would never give up.

00:12:57.068 --> 00:12:59.612
16-15, first string!

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:01.531
25 all, second string!

00:13:02.032 --> 00:13:04.784
37-36, first string!

00:13:08.413 --> 00:13:10.206
45 all, second string!

00:13:16.046 --> 00:13:17.339
Niou-<i>san</i>...

00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.257
This isn't good.

00:13:19.257 --> 00:13:21.092
The longer the game drags on,

00:13:21.092 --> 00:13:23.261
the greater the burden on his elbow.

00:13:23.762 --> 00:13:25.013
Stop, Niou!

00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:27.682
You'll break your elbow if you keep playing!

00:13:30.226 --> 00:13:32.729
He will not stop now.

00:13:34.439 --> 00:13:35.648
Why?

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.567
Why is he doing this?

00:13:48.411 --> 00:13:51.581
I was confident I could
form the strongest pair.

00:13:54.668 --> 00:13:57.629
I swore on my title, Niou the Illusionist,

00:13:57.629 --> 00:13:59.673
that I'd create the perfect Kunimitsu Tezuka.

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:04.678
49-48, second string!

00:14:10.058 --> 00:14:11.601
One more...

00:14:12.936 --> 00:14:15.522
Niou is willing to go this far for the team?

00:14:16.898 --> 00:14:17.899
Niou...

00:14:18.525 --> 00:14:22.404
Did you create the illusion of
Tezuka's mental fortitude, as well?

00:14:23.238 --> 00:14:26.324
I'd never fight this recklessly on my own.

00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:33.081
I'll keep hitting Phantoms,
or whatever else it takes,

00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:36.001
until I can't move my arm anymore!

00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:42.340
Niou-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:42.632 --> 00:14:43.550
Niou!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.429
The ball's still alive.

00:14:50.265 --> 00:14:53.601
Niou sacrificed his arm to
create this opportunity.

00:14:53.601 --> 00:14:55.770
I won't waste it!

00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:06.948
Atobe-<i>san</i>...

00:15:09.075 --> 00:15:13.121
You're the first one to recover
this quickly from the pressure.

00:15:15.749 --> 00:15:16.499
Atobe!

00:15:20.337 --> 00:15:22.380
K-Kabaji...

00:15:23.089 --> 00:15:27.427
Because the last point was scored by
an outsider, it violates the rules—

00:15:27.427 --> 00:15:28.428
Wait.

00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:30.597
You can count that point.

00:15:31.681 --> 00:15:33.767
Game and first set, second string!

00:15:33.767 --> 00:15:36.728
Atobe-Niou pair, seven games to six!

00:15:36.728 --> 00:15:38.021
Second set!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.149
Per the rules of the U-17 training camp,

00:15:41.149 --> 00:15:46.446
Munehiro Kabaji is ordered to leave the camp
for interfering with a match in progress.

00:15:49.741 --> 00:15:51.701
That was disgraceful.

00:15:52.202 --> 00:15:53.620
Get out of here, Kabaji.

00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:55.372
How can you say that?

00:15:55.372 --> 00:15:57.040
Kabaji did that for you!

00:15:57.332 --> 00:15:58.917
This is a serious match.

00:15:58.917 --> 00:16:01.461
I don't appreciate the help.

00:16:01.878 --> 00:16:02.921
Yes, sir.

00:16:04.798 --> 00:16:06.091
Idiot...

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:09.719
Can you still play, Niou?

00:16:09.719 --> 00:16:10.929
Pupinaccio.

00:16:11.304 --> 00:16:13.807
If I were ready to give up now...

00:16:16.059 --> 00:16:17.477
I'd still have a long way to go.

00:16:17.769 --> 00:16:19.562
What? Echizen?

00:16:19.562 --> 00:16:20.897
Why?

00:16:25.068 --> 00:16:26.778
A right Twist Serve...

00:16:27.612 --> 00:16:28.697
I get it!

00:16:28.697 --> 00:16:31.491
His right elbow hasn't suffered damage.

00:16:31.491 --> 00:16:33.201
He can still fight with his right.

00:16:34.369 --> 00:16:36.496
That's quite a sharp Twist,

00:16:36.496 --> 00:16:38.915
but not one I cannot return!

00:16:39.916 --> 00:16:40.917
He got it!

00:16:42.669 --> 00:16:43.753
Love-fifteen!

00:16:46.047 --> 00:16:48.425
I still have... a long way to go...

00:16:49.592 --> 00:16:50.593
Niou...

00:16:51.177 --> 00:16:54.180
You can't even stand anymore.

00:16:56.349 --> 00:16:57.392
Game, first string!

00:16:57.392 --> 00:16:59.019
Five games to love!

00:17:06.693 --> 00:17:08.570
Come on, you good-for-nothing.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.405
Time to switch sides.

00:17:10.405 --> 00:17:11.281
"First String"

00:17:11.281 --> 00:17:12.240
"First String"
Game, first string!

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.825
"First String"
Six games to love!

00:17:14.159 --> 00:17:16.286
One all, final set! Play!

00:17:18.246 --> 00:17:22.042
Niou can't serve or receive the ball anymore.

00:17:22.709 --> 00:17:27.839
If they don't start within 90 seconds of the
ref's call, their opponents get the point.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.425
In other words,

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:33.261
the second string can only take
games when it's Atobe's serve.

00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:35.972
Game, first string!

00:17:35.972 --> 00:17:37.182
One game to love!

00:17:37.557 --> 00:17:40.769
They can't possibly win now.

00:17:40.769 --> 00:17:43.605
But Atobe hasn't given up.

00:17:44.773 --> 00:17:47.317
Despite the overwhelming disadvantage,

00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:49.736
he's still looking straight ahead.

00:17:50.862 --> 00:17:56.117
He's not playing the beautiful
tennis he's been striving for.

00:17:56.951 --> 00:17:57.952
But...

00:18:01.664 --> 00:18:06.294
I can feel his passion more than ever.

00:18:07.837 --> 00:18:12.592
He's determined to win after
Niou sacrificed himself.

00:18:17.055 --> 00:18:21.559
His tenacity is what's
pushing him forward now.

00:18:25.647 --> 00:18:26.690
That's...

00:18:27.857 --> 00:18:29.317
Synchronization!

00:18:31.945 --> 00:18:33.238
That guy...

00:18:35.198 --> 00:18:39.577
He's been watching us while lying by the net!

00:18:40.912 --> 00:18:42.997
We fell for his trick!

00:18:44.207 --> 00:18:48.086
I've been watching your feet.

00:18:52.382 --> 00:18:58.221
--King! King! King!

00:18:58.221 --> 00:19:01.558
--Niou watches their movements
to find their blind spots.
--King! King! King!

00:19:01.558 --> 00:19:02.267
--King! King! King!

00:19:02.267 --> 00:19:05.854
--He instantaneously sends that
information to Atobe-kun.
--King! King! King!

00:19:05.854 --> 00:19:15.155
--King! King! King!

00:19:15.155 --> 00:19:17.032
--Interesting, interesting!
--King! King! King!

00:19:21.578 --> 00:19:25.457
Your brilliant play is intoxicating...

00:19:27.292 --> 00:19:29.419
Now freeze!

00:19:33.548 --> 00:19:35.216
Atobe Kingdom!

00:19:35.592 --> 00:19:37.135
I can see right through you!

00:19:38.178 --> 00:19:39.846
I can see the ball...

00:19:40.847 --> 00:19:42.474
But I can't react in time!

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.186
Sorry, but that's your
"absolute blind spot."

00:19:46.186 --> 00:19:50.398
In those positions, your skeletal
structures can't defend it.

00:19:51.149 --> 00:19:52.609
This ends now!

00:19:53.485 --> 00:19:56.154
Tsuki-<i>san</i>, the rest is up to you!

00:19:59.532 --> 00:20:01.284
Is he insane?

00:20:01.284 --> 00:20:03.370
He dislocated his arm!

00:20:24.557 --> 00:20:28.311
This... is a doubles match...

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:30.772
Game and match, second string!

00:20:30.772 --> 00:20:33.900
Atobe-Niou pair, two sets to one!

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:38.488
Seven games to six, love games to six,
seven games to six!

00:20:38.905 --> 00:20:42.659
That's one win against
the U-17 Japanese team!

00:20:42.992 --> 00:20:44.786
That was some good doubles.

00:20:44.786 --> 00:20:45.829
We lost.

00:20:46.579 --> 00:20:48.790
You demonstrated your tenacity.

00:20:51.126 --> 00:20:54.087
And you demonstrated the pride of the U-17.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.756
As promised,

00:20:57.799 --> 00:21:02.387
we'll take your spots on
the U-17 Japanese team.

00:21:02.846 --> 00:21:04.222
Of course.

00:21:04.222 --> 00:21:06.516
These pins are proof of your victory.

00:21:07.517 --> 00:21:08.226
Watch out!

00:21:10.979 --> 00:21:15.066
What fool dares to interfere
with my execution?

00:21:21.781 --> 00:21:24.117
I'll be waiting for you on the court.

00:21:24.117 --> 00:21:26.578
It'll be a bloodbath.

00:21:27.829 --> 00:21:29.372
Niou-<i>senpai</i>!

00:21:29.372 --> 00:21:30.373
Are you okay?

00:21:30.373 --> 00:21:31.750
It's nothing.

00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:33.418
Just a scratch.

00:21:35.378 --> 00:21:40.717
That pin was won by none other
than Masaharu Niou himself.

00:21:43.595 --> 00:21:45.430
He's everything I saw in him.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.357
"Next Time"

00:23:19.357 --> 00:23:20.567
"Next Time"
Marui-<i>kun</i>,

00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:21.860
"Next Time"
apparently we're the ideal doubles team.

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:24.154
apparently we're the ideal doubles team.

00:23:24.154 --> 00:23:27.323
Really? We're just playing like we always do.

00:23:27.323 --> 00:23:31.745
Yes, we're merely doing
our job, like we always do.

00:23:32.078 --> 00:23:33.621
Kiteretsu, something's not right.

00:23:33.621 --> 00:23:36.374
What? No such thing.

00:23:36.374 --> 00:23:39.794
"Side with the strong" is my motto.

00:23:39.794 --> 00:23:41.963
That's what I always do.

00:23:42.547 --> 00:23:46.343
"Betrayal and Negotiation"
The next episode of <i>New Prince</i>
<i>of Tennis </i>is: "Betrayal and Negotiation."

00:23:46.343 --> 00:23:48.480
"Betrayal and Negotiation"
Kiteretsu, you...
